  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a0a133cd-b1e3-492f-b6ce-24ba9f603a69-9893978_1.PNG\" style=\"width: 202px; height: 112px;\" /></p><p>Linear velocity at the distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;from the centre can be written as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>Therefore, induced EMF due to small element will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Integrating both sides, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
